# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Tentacle TV — optional settings for the stack with its database
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Nothing here is required: every line has a working default. To change a
#  value, copy this file to .env (next to compose.yaml), uncomment the line
#  and edit it, then run `docker compose up -d` again.
#  There is NO password to set: the database secrets are generated on the
#  first start and stay in the tentacle-secrets volume. Your Jellyfin
#  address and account are asked by the setup wizard, not here.

# ── Port on this machine ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TENTACLE_PORT=3000

# ── Time zone ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TZ=Europe/Paris

# ── User running Tentacle (never root) ────────────────────────────────────
# PUID=1000
# PGID=1000

# ── Image version ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TENTACLE_VERSION=latest
